    },
    {
      "title": "Waves enter the food",
      "text": "The oven makes microwave energy—waves that bounce off its metal walls and enter your food. The food absorbs some of that energy, especially in areas with water.",
      "imagePrompt": "Microwave waves bouncing inside a metal oven and entering a bowl of food"
