      "title": "Water molecules move",
      "text": "The waves’ changing electric field makes water molecules turn back and forth. Their motion and interactions pass energy around, a bit like a crowd jostling as it moves.",
      "imagePrompt": "Water molecules turning back and forth as waves pass through food"
    },
    {
      "title": "Motion becomes warmth",
      "text": "As the molecules interact, their extra motion spreads through the food as heat. Some spots absorb more energy than others, so a plate can have hot and cool patches.",
      "imagePrompt": "A plate of food with warm spots and cool spots shown in contrasting colors"
