      "title": "Stir, then let it rest",
      "text": "When you reheat leftovers, stirring moves hot and cool parts together. Letting the food rest also gives heat time to spread. That’s why stirring and waiting can make each bite more evenly warm.",
      "imagePrompt": "A person stirring reheated leftovers, with heat spreading evenly through the bowl"
    }
